{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Plan-review gate PASSES — attestation earned and durable\n\n    VERDICT: PASS\n    blocking: 0   advisory: 5   dropped: 0   indeterminate: 0\n    signature: signed=True\n    durable status: certified (ok=True)\n    verified_at_sha: 1bffbd586a2589bbaeab30e77453b26eebcf0f29\n\nConfirmed durable with the free no-LLM currency check (`review-plan --status`), not just from the\nrun's own exit code — a PASS whose attestation failed to persist would still leave the claim gate\nrefusing, and that distinction is worth checking rather than assuming.\n\nThis unblocks the `bugfix-size-attestation` finding on change 2684 (340 non-test lines against the\n150-line floor for a bug fix).\n\n### The arc, since the shape of it is the useful part\n\n| run | verdict | blocking findings |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 (MCP async) | run failed | `gate_congested` — infrastructure, no verdict |\n| 2 | BLOCK | 3 — ordering claim contradicted the script (x2), LEAD named an unbounded call that does not exist |\n| 3 | BLOCK | 1 — \"reserved tail budget\" named without an enforcement path |\n| 4 | **PASS** | 0 |\n\nEvery finding was about the **plan**, and every one was correct. None was about the implementation.\nThat is the honest summary: the code in 2684 has been right since patchset 2; the description was\ntelling a story the code had already outgrown, and each round the gate found the next place where\nthe plan asserted an outcome without a mechanism.\n\nThe last one was the most instructive. \"A reserved tail budget that no earlier section can spend\"\nis not achievable in straight-line bash by any preemptive means — once a `timeout`-wrapped call is\nblocked, nothing reclaims its budget. The gate was right to refuse a guarantee with no visible path\nto it. The implementation does the enforceable inverse (shrink each grant as the deadline\napproaches, so nothing can run into the reserved window), and the plan now says so explicitly, with\nthe derivation and the 1s-floor rationale.\n\n### Remaining\n\n- Bots to re-vote `LLM-Review` and `Verified` on patchset 2. CI's first attempt failed the\n  ticket-resolvability gate while the tickets branch was lagging behind a concurrent write; that\n  has since caught up and a recheck is running.\n- Not submitting."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788648569342962001,"uuid":"6cbdbdb8-c816-4ccc-88e0-f2bd4a4fce1b"}